description: 
globs: *.tsx,*.ts,*.js
alwaysApply: false
---
The application MUST support both light and dark themes, with a user-selectable toggle. Theme implementation will leverage next-themes for theme management and Tailwind CSS's darkMode: "class" strategy.

Package Installation: Install and configure the next-themes package.
Theme Provider: Wrap the root layout of the Next.js application with the ThemeProvider from next-themes, configuring it to use system preference as default and allow class-based switching.
Tailwind Configuration: Ensure tailwind.config.ts (or .js) is configured with darkMode: "class".
Theme Toggle UI: Implement a user-facing UI element (e.g., a button or dropdown, typically in the site header or user settings menu) that allows the user to explicitly choose "Light," "Dark," or "System" mode. This component will use the useTheme hook from next-themes to set the theme.
Styling: All custom components and styles MUST be designed to adapt to both light and dark modes. Use semantic color classes (e.g., `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `bg-muted`, `text-muted-foreground`, `bg-primary`, `text-primary-foreground`, `bg-destructive`, `text-destructive`, `bg-success`, `text-success`, `bg-warning`, `text-warning`, `bg-secondary`, `text-secondary`) that automatically adapt to the current theme. Avoid hardcoded color classes like `bg-gray-800` or `text-white`.
Shadcn/ui Compatibility: shadcn/ui components are built with theming in mind and should automatically adapt to the theme set by next-themes when CSS variables are used for colors (as configured during shadcn/ui init). Ensure that any custom overrides or compositions of shadcn/ui components also respect theme changes.
Persistence: The user's theme preference (Light, Dark, or System) MUST be persisted, typically via localStorage (which next-themes handles by default).
Example Theme Toggle Component Snippet (Illustrative):

TypeScript

// components/shared/ThemeToggle.tsx
"use client";

import { useTheme } from "next-themes";
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"; // Assuming Button component from shadcn/ui
import { MoonIcon, SunIcon } from "@radix-ui/react-icons"; // Or other icons

export function ThemeToggle() {
  const { theme, setTheme } = useTheme();

  return (
    <Button
      variant="ghost"
      size="icon"
      onClick={() => setTheme(theme === "light" ? "dark" : "light")}
    >
      <SunIcon className="h-[1.2rem] w-[1.2rem] rotate-0 scale-100 transition-all dark:-rotate-90 dark:scale-0" />
      <MoonIcon className="absolute h-[1.2rem] w-[1.2rem] rotate-90 scale-0 transition-all dark:rotate-0 dark:scale-100" />
      <span className="sr-only">Toggle theme</span>
    </Button>
  );
}

